    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d816">

                <pb facs="0763" n="591" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg591"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 124.62/45a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Willard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-26T11:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 26, 1917, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>285. When Mr. Gerard decides definitely
                    the date of his sailing for the United States, you should request the Spanish
                    Government to be so kind as to instruct the Spanish Ambassador in Berlin to
                    communicate that fact to the German Government for its information.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
